(8\) COMMON INSTRUCTOR Q&A \(PREPARED ANSWERS\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(Q: How are seats assigned automatically?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(A: The stored-procedure `sp_auto_allocate_seats` computes a list of bench-seat slots and) Tj
0 -14 Td
(assigns students by row-number ordering; it enforces capacity checks and uses transactions) Tj
0 -14 Td
(to avoid partial assignments.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(Q: How is faculty workload managed?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(A: `sp_assign_faculty_duties` picks available faculty with workload below a cap \(SQL) Tj
0 -14 Td
(cursor\) and increments workload on assignment; the UI calls it via `FacultyDutyService`.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(Q: Is authentication secure?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(A: Passwords are stored using PBKDF2 hashes via `PasswordUtil`. Legacy plaintext passwords) Tj
0 -14 Td
(are migrated on login; in production provide hashed passwords or reset them.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(Q: Can the application scale?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(A: This is a single-node Swing app backed by MySQL. Scaling to many users requires moving) Tj
0 -14 Td
(UI to a web UI or desktop clients coordinating via a server API.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
